            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "- **Perseverance has now driven a “marathon” on Mars.** NASA reported the rover reached **26.2 miles (42.195 km)** of total driving distance, and an MRO/HiRISE orbital image (June 13, 2026) shows the rover as a tiny speck plus the winding tracks of its route; the milestone was achieved on **sol 1,890**—faster than Opportunity’s time to the same distance. 【5:0†source】\n\n- **Perseverance recently imaged Earth disappearing behind Mars’ moon Phobos.** NASA posted a new Mastcam-Z composite (from **July 2, 2026**) and a feature (published **Aug 5, 2026**) describing the sequence in which **Earth appears as a point of light** that passes behind **Phobos** in the Martian sky. 【5:1†source】【5:3†source】\n\n- **Earlier in 2026, Perseverance completed the first AI-planned drives on another planet.** NASA/JPL described a demonstration where a **vision-capable generative AI** planned rover routes/waypoints (tests on **Dec 8 and 10, 2025**, announced **Jan 30, 2026**), which Perseverance then executed successfully. 【5:4†source】\n\nIf you tell me whether you want “latest news” as “last 7 days” vs “last 30–90 days,” I can summarize just that window.",
